Subject: [PATCH 13/22] write_file, edit_file: judge the workspace-relative
 path, and widen the list

Two QA findings from a second review pass:

The guard scanned every component of the resolved absolute path, and
worktree tab roots live under the main checkout's .gertie/worktrees/:
a worktree session's .gertie matched, and every write and edit a
worktree chat made was refused. Reproduced live before the fix (the
new test fails on the old guard with exactly that refusal). The guard
now judges the workspace-relative suffix: inside a tab, the tab's own
.git and .gertie stay protected, and its source files are ordinary
files.

The list widens to the config dirs other programs execute on the
user's behalf: .cargo/ (build wrappers run on the next cargo command),
.vscode/ tasks, .githooks/, .husky/, .devcontainer/. Same semantics:
refused at any depth, human edits by hand. The deny list's doc comment
is back on the deny list where it belongs.
